<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Meiji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Meiji Emperor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Meiji was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1867 to 1912. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a> of 1868 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> and restored imperial rule in his name, and his reign saw rapid modernisation, industrialisation and the building of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> into a major power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji.jpg" alt="Emperor Meiji" width="281" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uchida Kuichi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meiji_Emperor_(cropped)(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
